<task id="130" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H3: Graph app-reg port (Applications/ServicePrincipals/AppRoleAssignedTo/Oauth2PermissionGrants) + real consent verifier + KV writes + H10-idiom app-user assign</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-3 -- Identity + deploy</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Heaviest single port in the whole Phase G'' backlog per DS-1b (982-line script, 14 grants, consent flow) -- security-sensitive (Entra app registration, consent gate). FULL rigor.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Named explicitly in the parent task instructions' xhigh-effort exception list: 'complex-but-fully-specified... H3 heavy port' -- Sonnet @ xhigh.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>102, 103, 125, 126</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, option-d, sdk-port, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>14-20 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Port H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs's collaborator RegisterEntraAppRegScriptProvisioner (Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1, 982 lines: az ad app x19, az ad sp x2, az rest [Graph] x3, az keyvault secret x3, pac admin assign-app-to-environment x1) to Microsoft.Graph 6.x (already a BFF dependency at 6.5.0): Applications.PostAsync for app registration, ServicePrincipals for SP creation, AppRoleAssignedTo for the 14 grants, Oauth2PermissionGrants for delegated-permission wiring; KV writes via SecretClient (task 125's collaborator); the lone `pac admin assign-app-to-environment` call maps to the EXACT SAME Dataverse Web API app-user creation H10's collaborators already perform in-process (DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator.cs idiom -- REUSE it, do not reimplement). ALSO replace NullAdminConsentVerifier (which always returns Verified -- the consent gate can currently advance on fiction) with a real implementation: ONE Graph oauth2PermissionGrants query (~80 LOC per DS-1b) that actually checks whether admin consent was granted.

  **Auth-v4 coordination amendment (v3.5, 2026-08-19, per spec.md FR-39 + design.md §4.1 H3 row + §4D I6)**: this port MUST implement a runtime branch keyed on tenancy model, not a single unconditional app-reg-creation path. **Model 1**: the app-reg step is a NO-OP -- the shared multitenant BFF app-reg (`AzureADMultipleOrgs`) already exists; this branch instead (a) verifies the shared app-reg's 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants are current and (b) registers the customer tenant's service principal via the H0.5/D18 consent-callback path (coordinate with whichever task owns H0.5 -- do not reimplement consent-capture here). **Model 2**: creates a per-customer app-reg (as originally scoped) PLUS a federated identity credential (FIC) trusting the shared BFF UAMI, following auth-v4's §3.1 recipe (issuer = customer tenant OR Spaarke tenant depending on Spaarke-hosted vs customer-owned; subject = the UAMI's `principalId`, NOT `clientId`; audiences = `["api://AzureADTokenExchange"]`; retry logic for `AADSTS70021` propagation-delay errors, which are expected and NOT a failure on first occurrence). The app-reg selection logic itself (which branch runs) MUST derive from per-tenant request context with no default/fallback (I6 enforcement, design.md §4D).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Microsoft.Graph 6.x Applications/ServicePrincipals/AppRoleAssignments/Oauth2PermissionGrants SDK surface, Entra app-registration idempotency, admin-consent verification via oauth2PermissionGrants queries, and federated identity credential (FIC) creation for Managed-Identity-as-issuer patterns.</role>

  <goal>H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs's provisioner is a pure Microsoft.Graph SDK implementation with a tenancy-model runtime branch: **Model 1** verifies the shared app-reg's grants + registers customer-tenant trust via consent-callback (no new app-reg or FIC object created). **Model 2** performs app-reg ensure (idempotent create-if-absent), SP ensure, the 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants (per GraphAppRoles.cs's completed 11-of-14 catalog, task 005), Oauth2PermissionGrants wiring, KV writes, Dataverse app-user assignment via the REUSED H10 idiom, AND FIC creation trusting the shared BFF UAMI per auth-v4's §3.1 recipe with exchange-based verification (not creation-200 alone) and propagation-delay retry. A real AdminConsentVerifier replaces NullAdminConsentVerifier for the Model 2 path, performing a genuine Graph query proving consent was granted (not assumed). Recipe order per DS-4 §3 (Model 2 branch): Graph app ensure -&gt; 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants -&gt; consent gate -&gt; real Oauth2PermissionGrants verify -&gt; FIC creation + verify -&gt; KV writes -&gt; Dataverse app-user assign. The branch selection itself is I6-enforced: derived from per-tenant request context, no default/fallback.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-1b classifies H3's collaborator as 'the single heaviest port' (8-10 person-days per DS-1b §5) among all Class-A handlers. DS-4 §3 (H3 deep-dive) is explicit about the current defect's severity: 'POML 046 disclosed the Null consent verifier in scaffold headers, but the handler BEHAVES AS IF consent is verified (gate can advance on fiction).' This is distinct from an honestly-disclosed interim state -- it is a gate that silently passes. DS-4's recipe order (app ensure -&gt; 14 grants -&gt; consent gate -&gt; real verify -&gt; KV -&gt; Dataverse assign) is the authoritative sequencing this task follows. The 11-of-14 GraphAppRoles.cs GUIDs are already complete (task 005); the remaining 3 are a pre-existing, separately-tracked project risk item, not this task's scope to complete.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAdminConsentVerifier.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/NullAdminConsentVerifier.cs (retire)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/DataverseAppUserGraphParity/DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">wave-sequencing</dependency>
      <dependency task="103" status="pending">H3 keyed registration</dependency>
      <dependency task="125" status="pending">H4's SecretClient collaborator this task reuses for KV writes must exist</dependency>
      <dependency task="126" status="pending">H4's real-value-sourcing fix must have landed so the KV values H3 reads/writes are functional, not placeholder</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.1b">Handler runtime classification (Option D hybrid, DS-1b Sec.2): 12 handlers are pure .NET SDK/REST under DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the L2 UAMI (Class A); H14a is the sole Class-C residual (Exchange sidecar); H7/H10/H11/H12c are already native. No ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may remain in this handler's target state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules (post-line-254 block)">No new ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may be introduced by this task. Option D's entire point is deleting the pwsh/az/pac dependency from the L2 runtime, not adding to it (the sole designed exception is the H14a Exchange sidecar).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §3 H3 deep-dive">Recipe order is binding, not incidental: Graph app ensure -&gt; 14 AppRoleAssignedTo grants -&gt; consent gate -&gt; real Oauth2PermissionGrants verify -&gt; KV writes -&gt; Dataverse app-user assign via the H10 idiom. Do not reorder (e.g., writing KV secrets before consent verification would leak a functional secret before the consent gate has genuinely passed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="this project's CLAUDE.md MUST rules">MUST complete 11 of 14 null AppRoleId GUIDs in GraphAppRoles.cs BEFORE first production customer -- already done (task 005). This task consumes the completed catalog; it does NOT re-verify or re-complete the GUIDs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §3">REUSE the H10 Dataverse app-user creation idiom verbatim for the pac admin assign-app-to-environment replacement -- do not write a second, parallel implementation of the same find-by-applicationid/create/role-associate sequence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-39 + design.md §4.1 H3 row (added v3.5 2026-08-19, auth-v4 coordination)">The Model 1 vs Model 2 runtime branch is BINDING, not optional scope. Model 1 MUST NOT create a new app-reg or FIC object -- doing so would violate the spec.md MUST-rule split (Model 1 = single shared app-reg only). Model 2's FIC creation follows auth-v4's §3.1 recipe exactly (subject = UAMI principalId, not clientId -- this is the documented most-common misconfiguration trap).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §4D invariant I6 (Model 1 only, added v3.5)">The code path selecting which app-reg branch to run (Model 1 no-op vs Model 2 create) MUST take tenant/tenancy-model context as an explicit parameter with no default or fallback value -- this is the exact call site the new `Spaarke.ArchTests.TenantIsolation.I6_ObApp*` ArchTest will scan.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §3.2 (coordination note, notes/AUTH-V4-CHANGE-REQUEST-RESPONSE.md)">If `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI` has already landed a FIC-creation extension to `scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1` by the time this task executes, INVOKE that extended script/logic rather than duplicating FIC-creation logic independently (soft dependency -- check before authoring FIC creation from scratch).</constraint>
  </constraints>

